===========================================================================
Academic & Methodological Attributions
===========================================================================

CausalSieve is an independent clean-room C++20 and zero-dependency Python
implementation building upon foundational published results in time-series
causality, online estimation, robust statistics, sequential testing, and
error-bounded stream compression:

1. Vector Autoregression & Conditional Granger Causality
   - C. W. J. Granger, "Investigating Causal Relations by Econometric Models
     and Cross-spectral Methods," Econometrica, 37(3):424-438, 1969.
   - C. A. Sims, "Macroeconomics and Reality," Econometrica, 48(1):1-48, 1980.
   - Block-Schur complement exact leave-one-block-out ridge objective identity
     over recursively maintained inverse Gram matrices (Sherman-Morrison /
     Recursive Least Squares).

2. Contemporaneous Non-Gaussian Causal Orientation (LiNGAM)
   - S. Shimizu, P. O. Hoyer, A. Hyvarinen, and A. Kerminen, "A Linear
     Non-Gaussian Acyclic Model for Causal Discovery," JMLR, 7:2003-2030, 2006.
   - A. Hyvarinen and S. M. Smith, "Pairwise Likelihood Ratios for Estimation
     of Non-Gaussian Structural Equation Models," JMLR, 14:111-152, 2013.

3. Robust M-Estimation & Bounded-Influence Regression
   - P. J. Huber, "Robust Estimation of a Location Parameter," Annals of
     Mathematical Statistics, 35(1):73-101, 1964.
   - C. L. Mallows, "On Some Topics in Robustness," Bell Laboratories Technical
     Memorandum, 1975.

4. Anytime-Valid Sequential Testing & E-Processes
   - J. Ville, "Etude critique de la notion de collectif," Gauthier-Villars,
     1939.
   - A. Ramdas, P. Grunwald, V. Vovk, and G. Shafer, "Game-Theoretic Statistics
     and Safe Anytime-Valid Inference," Statistical Science, 38(4):576-601, 2023.
   - E. Hazan, A. Agarwal, and S. Kale, "Logarithmic Regret Algorithms for
     Online Convex Optimization" (Online Newton Step), Machine Learning,
     69(2-3):169-192, 2007.

5. Randomized Inverse Drift Verification
   - R. Freivalds, "Fast Probabilistic Algorithms," Mathematical Foundations
     of Computer Science, LNCS 74:57-69, 1979.

6. Error-Bounded Piecewise Linear Stream Compression
   - H. Elmeleegy, A. K. Elmagarmid, E. Cecchet, W. G. Aref, and W. Zwaenepoel,
     "Online Piece-Wise Linear Approximation of Numerical Streams with
     Precision Guarantees" (Swing Filter), PVLDB, 2(1):145-156, 2009.

